(Reservoir station training notes) Tj
T*
(The station stores clean water for a demonstration garden.) Tj
T*
(Its three components are the intake screen, reservoir, and outlet valve.) Tj
T*
(The intake screen catches leaves before water enters the reservoir.) Tj
T*
(The reservoir stores water. Its maximum capacity is 100 litres.) Tj
T*
(The outlet valve controls water flowing from the reservoir to the garden.) Tj
T*
(The amber indicator means the reservoir holds less than 20 litres.) Tj
T*
(The red indicator means the reservoir holds more than 80 litres.) Tj
T*
(The green indicator means the reservoir holds 20 through 80 litres.) Tj
T*
(To start the station, inspect the intake screen first.) Tj
T*
(Next, open the intake valve. Then fill the reservoir to 50 litres.) Tj
T*
(Finally, open the outlet valve to send water to the garden.) Tj
T*
(Inspect the screen every morning. Remove trapped leaves by hand.) Tj
T*
(Keep the outlet closed whenever the amber indicator is on.) Tj
T*
(Close the intake valve whenever the red indicator is on.) Tj
T*
(Record the reservoir level and indicator colour in the daily log.) Tj
ET
endstream
